  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758520,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "'96 Zenkoku Koukou Soccer Senshuken is a thrilling soccer game for the Super Nintendo Entertainment System, continuing the legacy of *Zenkoku Koukou Soccer* and *Zenkoku Koukou Soccer 2*. Immerse yourself in the high-stakes world of a national high school soccer tournament, following the journey of a single player and their team as they battle for victory. \n\nThe game offers a unique, horizontal perspective, fixing the player's viewpoint rather than allowing direct control of all players. Customize your protagonist's appearance and hone their skills through training exercises to maximize their performance on the pitch.  Experience a compelling story mode that focuses on the protagonist's progression through the tournament rounds. \n\nDrawing inspiration from titles like *Hat Trick Hero* and *Top Striker*, *'96 Zenkoku Koukou Soccer Senshuken* allows you to embody a single player, a feature that foreshadowed the career modes found in later EA Sports games. Featuring teams from across Japan, and even including a nod to real-life soccer star Shunsuke Nakamura, this sequel introduces significant improvements, including character creation and coach feedback, elevating the gameplay experience."
    },
